//! task: fix
//! ask: Return `a` when it exceeds 10, else 0.
//! expect: EXS-E0201,EXS-E0307
//! primary: EXS-E0201
//! refs: §8.4, §8.5
//! explain: This is the C or Rust spelling. In Exsecutor `if` and `return` are not keywords at all, only ordinary identifiers, so the parser does not recognise a condition or a return; the spellings are `si` and `redde`, and `>` is the word `gt`. The `EXS-E0307` is cascade: with no `redde` recognised the function appears to fall off its end.

publica functio maxima(a: u64) -> u64 {
    if a > 10 { return a; }
}
//@ fixed
publica functio maxima(a: u64) -> u64 {
    si a gt 10 { redde a; }
    redde 0;
}
